OPTIONAL BASEMAPS

The default provider is USGS Topo (United States). Attribution:
  U.S. Geological Survey, National Geospatial Program
  https://www.usgs.gov/faqs/what-are-terms-uselicensing-map-services-and-data-national-map

OpenStreetMap is an alternative provider.
Map data © OpenStreetMap contributors. Attribution and licence information:
  https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright

Basemap starts off when no choice has been saved; existing explicit choices are
preserved. The first new enable explains the provider's receipt of the user's
IP address and viewed map area and requires confirmation. The remembered switch
is available below ride maps and in Map settings. When enabled, the app loads
only the visible map area. It identifies
requests with an application User-Agent, caches tiles with response metadata
and uses conditional revalidation. It does not bulk-download or prefetch map
regions. Cached tiles are a viewing cache, not a promised offline map package.
OpenStreetMap tile policy: https://operations.osmfoundation.org/policies/tiles/

A different HTTPS tile provider can be configured in the app. Its service, usage
and attribution terms apply to that provider's content. Map tiles and map data
are separate from the application source and are not relicensed by the MIT
licence reproduced above. Scooter controls and recording do not depend on a
street-map provider.


